{
    "openapi": "3.1.0",
    "info": {
        "title": "Paer Quotations API",
        "description": "\n> ## \ud83d\udc4b Three APIs, one site\n>\n> This documentation site bundles **three Paer APIs** under a single nav.\n> Right now you're looking at the **Quotes API**. To see the others\n> (**User API**, **Beneficiary API**), look for the **dropdown at the\n> top of the left sidebar** \u2014 just above the search box. It currently\n> reads **\"Quotes API \u25be\"**. Click it to switch.\n\n**Paer** is a Danish B2B cross-border payments platform. We let you send\nmoney to a counterparty abroad at near-mid-market FX, with settlement\ntimes ranging from a few seconds for our instant corridors to a few\nhours for SWIFT-correspondent destinations.\n\nThis is the **Quotes API** \u2014 the entry-point for every cross-border send.\nYou ask \"how much will it cost to send X EUR to Brazil right now?\", we\nreturn a price-locked quote good for 5\u201330 seconds, and you accept it to\ntrigger settlement. The other two services in the dropdown handle the\nplumbing: **User API** (signup / login / API keys / KYB) and\n**Beneficiary API** (counterparties + sanctions / PEP / adverse-media).\nAll three speak the same auth model \u2014 one `X-API-Key` works everywhere.\n\n## What you can build\n\n- **Pay a foreign supplier**: get a DKK\u2192USD or DKK\u2192BRL quote, accept it,\n  Paer settles. One API call to price, one to commit.\n- **Embedded payments in your product**: lock a quote at checkout, accept\n  it when the customer clicks pay. The 5-second TTL protects both sides\n  against mid-flight FX moves.\n- **Treasury automation**: sweep DKK\u2192EUR for a Danish business at\n  zero spread (we market-make this leg via Nationalbanken).\n- **Vibe-coding an MVP**: hand your LLM the URL `https://docs.paer.dk`\n  and it has the full spec, request shapes, and example payloads. Auth\n  is one header (`X-API-Key`), JSON in / JSON out, no SDK required.\n\n## Getting started\n\n```\n1. Sign up at https://app.paer.dk     \u2190 creates your company shell + first user\n2. Verify your email + enrol MFA       \u2190 user-api guides you through this\n3. Mint an API key in the dashboard    \u2190 starts with \"paer_sk_...\"\n4. Call /v1/quotes (this service) with that key\n```\n\n### Your first quote\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://api.paer.dk/v1/quotes \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: paer_sk_...\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"sell_currency\": \"DKK\",\n    \"buy_currency\": \"EUR\",\n    \"buy_country\":   \"DE\",\n    \"sell_amount\":   \"10000.00\"\n  }'\n```\n\nYou get back `mid_market_rate`, `rate` (what you actually get), `spread_bps`\n(how far that is from mid), `flat_fee_amount`, and a `quote_id`. Accept\nit within the TTL by `POST /v1/quotes/{id}/accept`.\n\n## Auth in one paragraph\n\nEvery authenticated endpoint takes `X-API-Key: paer_sk_...`. Keys are\nminted by the **User API** (see the sidebar) and tied to a user inside a\ncompany. The user has a role: **A** (full write), **B** (write requires a\nsecond A/B signature), or **C** (read-only). For solo-founder pilots, you\nget an A-key and never think about it again.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- All money amounts are decimal strings \u2014 never floats. `\"10000.00\"`, not `10000`.\n- All currencies are ISO 4217 (`DKK`, `EUR`, `USD`). All countries ISO 3166 alpha-2 (`DK`, `DE`, `BR`).\n- All datetimes UTC ISO 8601 with `+00:00`.\n- `X-Request-ID` is echoed if you supply one; minted otherwise. Use it to\n  correlate logs across services.\n",
        "version": "0.1.0"
    },
    "paths": {
        "/health": {
            "get": {
                "summary": "Health",
                "description": "Liveness + DB connectivity probe.\n\nApp Runner's health check treats any non-200 as unhealthy and will pull the\ninstance from the load balancer after the configured unhealthy threshold.\nReturning 503 when the DB is unreachable is what we want \u2014 better to fail\nclosed than keep routing traffic to a pod that can't persist quotes.",
                "operationId": "health_health_get",
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "Successful Response",
                        "content": {
                            "application/json": {
                                "schema": {
                                    "additionalProperties": {
                                        "type": "string"
                                    },
                                    "type": "object",
                                    "title": "Response Health Health Get"
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        },
        "/v1/fx/corridors": {
            "get": {
                "tags": [
                    "fx"
                ],
                "summary": "Get Corridors",
                "description": "Complete corridor catalog in one call.\n\nOn the sell side: the two currencies Paer accepts as source (EUR, DKK)\nand the pay-in rail(s) for each.\n\nOn the buy side: every currency we can quote against, each with one or\nmore destination-country entries, and an optional `other_country_fallback`\ndescribing what happens if the customer wants the currency paid into a\nbank outside that currency's native country (routed via SWIFT).\n\nRouting partner identity is deliberately not in this response \u2014 which\nunderlying provider handles which corridor is implementation detail\nthat Paer manages on your behalf.",
                "operationId": "get_corridors_v1_fx_corridors_get",
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "Successful Response",
                        "content": {
                            "application/json": {
                                "schema": {
                                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CorridorsResponse"
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        },
        "/v1/fx/rate": {
            "get": {
                "tags": [
                    "fx"
                ],
                "summary": "Get Rate",
                "description": "Direct mid-market rate lookup. Not used in quote creation (quotes\ncompute their own mid + spread) \u2014 exposed for debugging + reference.",
                "operationId": "get_rate_v1_fx_rate_get",
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "name": "from",
                        "in": "query",
                        "required": true,
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "minLength": 3,
                            "maxLength": 3,
                            "title": "From"
                        }
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "to",
                        "in": "query",
                        "required": true,
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "minLength": 3,
                            "maxLength": 3,
                            "title": "To"
                        }
                    }
                ],
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "Successful Response",
                        "content": {
                            "application/json": {
                                "schema": {
                                    "type": "object",
                                    "additionalProperties": {
                                        "type": "string"
                                    },
                                    "title": "Response Get Rate V1 Fx Rate Get"
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    },
                    "422": {
                        "description": "Validation Error",
                        "content": {
                            "application/json": {
                                "schema": {
                                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        },
        "/v1/quotes": {
            "post": {
                "tags": [
                    "quotes"
                ],
                "summary": "Create Quote",
                "description": "Request a live FX quote.\n\nBody contract:\n- `sell_currency` + `buy_currency` \u2014 required, 3-letter ISO 4217.\n- Exactly ONE of `sell_amount` / `buy_amount` (422 otherwise).\n- `destination_country` + `payout_method` \u2014 optional; see `GET /v1/fx/corridors`.\n\nAuthentication is optional. Quotes created without an API key can be\ninspected but not accepted (rule 5). Authenticated quotes are tied to\nthe caller's `company_id` and `user_id` (via paer-user-api introspection)\nand can be accepted by any A/B-role user from the same company.",
                "operationId": "create_quote_v1_quotes_post",
                "requestBody": {
                    "content": {
                        "application/json": {
                            "schema": {
                                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/QuoteCreate"
                            }
                        }
                    },
                    "required": true
                },
                "responses": {
                    "201": {
                        "description": "Successful Response",
                        "content": {
                            "application/json": {
                                "schema": {
                                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/QuoteResponse"
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    },
                    "422": {
                        "description": "Validation Error",
                        "content": {
                            "application/json": {
                                "schema": {
                                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                },
                "security": [
                    {
                        "ApiKey": []
                    }
                ]
            }
        },
        "/v1/quotes/{quote_id}": {
            "get": {
                "tags": [
                    "quotes"
                ],
                "summary": "Get Quote",
                "description": "Fetch a quote by ID.\n\n`status` reflects real-time state \u2014 a quote stored as `\"live\"` whose\n`expires_at` has passed returns `\"expired\"` here (the DB transition\nhappens lazily on the next accept attempt; this read does not mutate).",
                "operationId": "get_quote_v1_quotes__quote_id__get",
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "name": "quote_id",
                        "in": "path",
                        "required": true,
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "title": "Quote Id"
                        }
                    }
                ],
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "Successful Response",
                        "content": {
                            "application/json": {
                                "schema": {
                                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/QuoteResponse"
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    },
                    "422": {
                        "description": "Validation Error",
                        "content": {
                            "application/json": {
                                "schema": {
                                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        },
        "/v1/quotes/{quote_id}/accept": {
            "post": {
                "tags": [
                    "quotes"
                ],
                "summary": "Accept Quote",
                "description": "Accept a live quote.\n\nRole gates (paer-user-api):\n  - C-role caller: 403 view_only_role_cannot_accept\n  - A-role caller: solo authority \u2014 applies immediately (200)\n  - B-role caller: signature recorded; quote stays in\n    `pending_signatures` (response code 202) until a second distinct\n    A or B from the same company also calls this endpoint.\n\nIdempotency-Key scope: keyed by `(idempotency_key, user_id, company_id)`.\nA retry from a different device (same user, different api key) hits the cache.",
                "operationId": "accept_quote_v1_quotes__quote_id__accept_post",
                "security": [
                    {
                        "ApiKey": []
                    }
                ],
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "name": "quote_id",
                        "in": "path",
                        "required": true,
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "title": "Quote Id"
                        }
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Idempotency-Key",
                        "in": "header",
                        "required": false,
                        "schema": {
                            "anyOf": [
                                {
                                    "type": "string"
                                },
                                {
                                    "type": "null"
                                }
                            ],
                            "title": "Idempotency-Key"
                        }
                    }
                ],
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "Successful Response",
                        "content": {
                            "application/json": {
                                "schema": {
                                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/QuoteResponse"
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    },
                    "422": {
                        "description": "Validation Error",
                        "content": {
                            "application/json": {
                                "schema": {
                                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        },
        "/": {
            "get": {
                "summary": "Root",
                "operationId": "root__get",
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "Successful Response",
                        "content": {
                            "application/json": {
                                "schema": {
                                    "additionalProperties": {
                                        "type": "string"
                                    },
                                    "type": "object",
                                    "title": "Response Root  Get"
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    },
